hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1497.1","Malik spoke to me about a man who wrote a kitaba for his slave for gold or silver and stipulated against him in his kitaba a journey"
"1497.2","Malik spoke to me about a man who wrote a kitaba for his slave for gold or silver and stipulated against him in his kitaba a journey"
"1498.1","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab used to say"
"1498.2","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab used to say"
"1499.1","[1499] And he related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab, Sulayman ibn Yasar, and Rabi'a ibn..."
"1499.2","[1499] And he related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab, Sulayman ibn Yasar, and Rabi'a ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman used to say: ""The blood-money for accidental killing is twenty bint makhad (one-year female camel), twenty bint labun (two-year female camel), twenty ibn labun (two-year male camel), twenty hiqqa (three-year female camel), and twenty jadha'a (four-year female camel)."" Muwatta of Imam Malik, Hadith: 1499, Arabic Hadith."
